# Credentials for the data stack. Copy to .env beside this file, fill in,
# chmod 600. docker compose reads it automatically.
#
# NEVER commit the filled-in file, and never put these in a unit file either:
# the MinIO credentials have already been rotated once, after being exposed in a
# world-readable unit.

MINIO_ROOT_USER=
MINIO_ROOT_PASSWORD=

# The rest of docker-compose.yml's variables carry defaults, so they only need
# to be set when this machine differs from them. Listed here because a variable
# with a default is invisible until the day someone needs to change it.
#
# POSTGRES_DB=arcana
# POSTGRES_USER=arcana
# POSTGRES_PASSWORD=arcana
#
# The published host port for Postgres. The test gate in
# services/decision-engine/internal/store/db_required_test.go reads this too, to
# know where to look for a database before deciding whether a skip is honest.
# HOST_POSTGRES=5432
